# Product Architect Phase

Full spec: `docs/product/KEBU-PRODUCT-ARCHITECT-PHASE.md`

## First instruction (before any code)

**STOP. DO NOT WRITE APPLICATION CODE.**

Reverse-engineer the product category into a **complete implementation blueprint**:

IA · navigation · screens · journeys · features · interactions · components · data model · state · permissions · loading/empty/error/success · responsive · keyboard · backend · integrations · tests.

**Do not simplify** into a prototype. **Do not substitute visual approximation for functionality.**

Reference **dossiers** (`docs/reference/*/PRODUCT-BENCHMARK.md`) — **not** product names alone.

## Product density

Professional application density — **not** landing-page prototype (oversized cards, giant buttons, fake simplicity).

## Maturity target (not clone)

Shopify-**level** UX · Canva-**level** tooling · Spotify-**level** discovery — **our** identity, not Frankenstein copy.

## After blueprint only

**Vertical slices** end-to-end (Supabase) — never entire frontend then backend shell.

**Design QA loop** — inspect running app; fix spacing/hierarchy/density until standard met. **If it looks AI-generated or MVP-ish, failed.**

**Fewer complete features > many fake screens.** No MVP aesthetics unless explicitly requested.

Broken dependency → **STOP and repair** (`kebu-master-engineering.mdc`).
